tr.td:
Any one or more of the following purposes to enable or assist the authority to perform any of its functions under an Act:
(a) monitoring compliance with an obligation or requirement;
(b) enforcing compliance with an obligation or requirement, including:
(i) investigating or enforcing breaches of a civil penalty provision;
(ii) applying for civil penalty orders or injunctions;
(iii) issuing infringement notices;
(iv) accepting or enforcing undertakings relating to compliance with an obligation or requirement;
(c) protecting public revenue;
(d) granting a licence, right or other authorisation;
(e) a purpose prescribed by the regulations.
However, a disclosure under this item must not be for the purpose of assisting in the prevention, investigation or prosecution of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, or of a State or Territory
